N2  - This cross-sectional study examined whether developmental assets moderate the relationship between intersectional discrimination and mental health among B [...]

Impact Statement
Black sexual minority men often face overlapping racism and homophobia that adversely affect their mental health. This study demonstrates that stronger developmental assets-such as supportive relationships, opportunities for engagement, and a positive sense of identity-can mitigate some of these detrimental effects, highlighting important areas for intervention by schools, families, and communities. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2026 APA, all rights reserved)
