N2  - Objective: This study aimed to determine the rates, chronicity, and correlates of nightmares and insomnia, alone and in combination, in U.S. Army personne [...]

Impact Statement
Insomnia (trouble falling or staying asleep) and nightmares (repeated distressing dreams about military experiences) were reported by about one third (32%-38%) both before and after deployments in support of Operation Iraqi Freedom and Operation Enduring Freedom from 2010 to 2016. These sleep problems alone and especially when combined were linked to mental health problems like anxiety, anger, and posttraumatic stress disorder. Systematic assessment and treatment of insomnia and nightmares could be a practical way to improve sleep and overall mental health in service members. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2026 APA, all rights reserved)
